<title>BRAZIL: Brazil likely to scrap PROER bank program by June.</title>
<headline>Brazil likely to scrap PROER bank program by June.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's Central Bank is likely to scrap the PROER program designed to encourage bank mergers and acquisitions by the end of June, a Central Bank spokesman said.</p>
<p>The spokesman confirmed newspaper reports Friday that the PROER program, created in November 1995 to strenghten a then-weak banking system, could be scrapped because the risk of a banking crisis no longer exists.</p>
<p>Central Bank president Gustavo Loyola told newspapers that the Central Bank is now concerned about the future of state banks.</p>
</text>
